Subject: [PATCH 0075] FEXCore: use operand width for BLSR/BLSMSK CF

Backport of upstream FEX 635befb4c802432897a7a5bd28e6755f29c044a4.
Upstream MIT; dispatcher retains its SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT header.
The CF zero-test must ignore bits 63:32 for a 32-bit source. The result
calculation and all undefined-flag choices are unchanged. No new gate.

Family: BMI1 low-bit isolate/reset/mask, 32/64-bit register and memory source
Members: BLSI, BLSR, BLSMSK (VEX.NDD.LZ.0F38.W0/W1 F3 /1,/2,/3)
Trigger: c4e278f3d0; RAX=deadbeef00000000; BLSMSK32 must set CF=1
Coverage:
  [x] BLSR32/BLSMSK32: existing decode/IR/JIT, CF test corrected to Size
  [x] BLSR64/BLSMSK64: unchanged Size=i64Bit, covered by hardware rows
  [x] BLSI32/BLSI64: audited, CF uses result ZF, no source-width defect
  [x] Memory forms and source/destination aliases: private family probe
  [ ] Separate interpreter: not applicable; production path is FEX IR/AArch64
Regression: high32/low32 zero, nonzero, sign-bit/max, both incoming CF values
InstructionCountCI: all four upstream cmp x6 -> cmp w6 expectations retained
Audit completed: yes (see FAMILY-AUDIT.md and measured family receipts)
Product installation: skipped; ENGINE-108 admission belongs to curator

--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
@@ -1819,7 +1819,7 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::BLSMSKBMIOp(OpcodeArgs) {
   InvalidatePF_AF();
 
   // CF set according to the Src
-  auto CFInv = To01(OpSize::i64Bit, Src);
+  auto CFInv = To01(Size, Src);
 
   // The output of BLSMSK is always nonzero, so TST will clear Z (along with C
   // and O) while setting S.
@@ -1837,7 +1837,7 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::BLSRBMIOp(OpcodeArgs) {
 
   StoreResultGPR(Op, Result);
 
-  auto CFInv = To01(OpSize::i64Bit, Src);
+  auto CFInv = To01(Size, Src);
 
   SetNZ_ZeroCV(Size, Result);
   SetCFInverted(CFInv);
